type Completion = string Completion is a string that can be used for
completions
.IP
.EX
two formats are supported:
  \- the completion choice
  \- the completion choice with a textual description (separated by a TAB).

CompletionWithDesc can be used to create a completion string with a textual
description.

Note: Go type alias is used to provide a more descriptive name in the
documentation, but any string can be used.
.EE
.PP
func AppendActiveHelp(compArray []Completion, activeHelpStr string)
[]Completion AppendActiveHelp adds the specified string to the specified
array to be used as ActiveHelp.
Such strings will be processed by the completion script and will be
shown as ActiveHelp to the user.
The array parameter should be the array that will contain the
completions.
This function can be called multiple times before and/or after
completions are added to the array.
Each time this function is called with the same array, the new
ActiveHelp line will be shown below the previous ones when completion is
triggered.
.PP
func CompletionWithDesc(choice string, description string) Completion
CompletionWithDesc returns a Completion with a description by using the
TAB delimited format.
.PP
type CompletionFunc = func(cmd *Command, args []string, toComplete
string) ([]Completion, ShellCompDirective) CompletionFunc is a function
that provides completion results.
.PP
func FixedCompletions(choices []Completion, directive
ShellCompDirective) CompletionFunc FixedCompletions can be used to
create a completion function which always returns the same results.
.IP
.EX
This method returns a function that satisfies CompletionFunc It can be used
with Command.RegisterFlagCompletionFunc and for [Command.ValidArgsFunction].
.EE
.PP
type CompletionOptions struct { // DisableDefaultCmd prevents Cobra from
creating a default `completion' command DisableDefaultCmd bool //
DisableNoDescFlag prevents Cobra from creating the
`\(enno\-descriptions' flag // for shells that support completion
descriptions DisableNoDescFlag bool // DisableDescriptions turns off all
completion descriptions for shells // that support them
DisableDescriptions bool // HiddenDefaultCmd makes the default
`completion' command hidden HiddenDefaultCmd bool //
DefaultShellCompDirective sets the ShellCompDirective that is returned
// if no special directive can be determined DefaultShellCompDirective
*ShellCompDirective } CompletionOptions are the options to control shell
completion
